{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","id":"pg_11a9aca38de65343a2ea7f38ec2ed9e9","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/neovateai-neovate-code-docs-development-commands-md-0a24b363ecbe-7f38ec2ed9e9.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_764bcaac48e958ebbd50d6c3918b44bd"],"title":"neovateai/neovate-code/docs/development_commands.md @ 0a24b363ecbe","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ce59c42ae9eb4d649d02ef1a15400170ec5236e0c4612d006d3b1da880fb160"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned BackgroundTaskManager stores tasks in a Map with fields id, command, pid, optional pgid, status (running/completed/killed/failed), createdAt, output, and exitCode, generating ids prefixed 'task_'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_34f54d8b9a5ebf57910ac32e7949fcbf7840411d305551770e9e13772a8201f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Because the bash background execution material is a step-by-step implementation plan with TDD instructions, the described tools and behavior appear to be proposed rather than verified as already shipped in this snapshot."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7daba09d4c9d196c92e3a6214a8fbb587eeba46a6dd793b3e26ef45728990dd1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned bash_output tool takes a task_id and returns the task's command, status, PID, creation time, accumulated output, and exit code when set."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae7cc88cc46ec8df800819b1cbc2174a01476345df240f1722a1aeb88cb60b23"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Background detection runs a command in background if user-requested, or if elapsed time exceeds a 2000ms threshold with output and the command root matches a dev-command list (npm, pnpm, yarn, node, python, go, cargo, docker, vite, jest, pytest, and others)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6ef33a419da9b6a4754696182b48949da68678461ff6d67210f042d8e355858"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A 2025-01-27 plan proposes background bash execution so the LLM can monitor and control long-running development tasks, extending the bash tool with a BackgroundTaskManager plus bash_output and kill_bash tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cbf9163feda76f637f22834f0145cccd52552d5ab51967614e85160c15d985a1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The plan adds a run_in_background boolean parameter to the bash tool and documents that dev-pattern commands auto-move to background after 2 seconds if producing output, returning a task_id for bash_output and kill_bash."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dde1f11e32a47a9519330fb4b72cd4f5db5114039e8d2fce8f5d25c6f58519c2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In the planned design, bash_output requires no approval (category 'read', needsApproval returns false), while kill_bash refuses to terminate tasks whose status is not 'running'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc2956f870a29f84b57798055cc5fa63e7450eb920f6e4f6548956a723ea6134"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The planned killTask uses taskkill on Windows; otherwise it signals the process group with SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 200ms if still running, falling back to killing the pid directly."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ce59c42ae9eb4d649d02ef1a15400170ec5236e0c4612d006d3b1da880fb160","clm_34f54d8b9a5ebf57910ac32e7949fcbf7840411d305551770e9e13772a8201f5","clm_7daba09d4c9d196c92e3a6214a8fbb587eeba46a6dd793b3e26ef45728990dd1","clm_ae7cc88cc46ec8df800819b1cbc2174a01476345df240f1722a1aeb88cb60b23","clm_b6ef33a419da9b6a4754696182b48949da68678461ff6d67210f042d8e355858","clm_cbf9163feda76f637f22834f0145cccd52552d5ab51967614e85160c15d985a1","clm_dde1f11e32a47a9519330fb4b72cd4f5db5114039e8d2fce8f5d25c6f58519c2","clm_fc2956f870a29f84b57798055cc5fa63e7450eb920f6e4f6548956a723ea6134"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","created_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7","id":"pg_49d5e23b23585c219ddb6e12440c6520","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/neovateai-neovate-code-docs-designs-2025-01-27-bash-background-executi-6e12440c6520.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_713f4f24bf0c550fb7498b9a778269e1"],"title":"neovateai/neovate-code/docs/designs/2025-01-27-bash-background-execution.md @ 0a24b363ecbe","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:22:03Z","updated_by_operation":"op_83e063e10e794567a685a4233f87a7c7"}
